}}{\footerl \pard \s2 \ql \sl200 \tqc\tx4147 \tqr\tx8306 {\f1 \fs20 \par 
}}\pard \s3 \ql \sl200 \sb240 \sa60 \tql\tx360 \tql\tx720 \tql\tx1080 \tql\tx1440 \tql\tx1800 \tql\tx2160 \tql\tx2520 \tql\tx2880 \tql\tx3240 \tql\tx3600 \tql\tx3960 \tql\tx4320 \tql\tx4680 \tql\tx5040 \tql\tx5400 \tql\tx5760 \tql\tx6120 \tql\tx6480 \tql\tx6840 \tql\tx7200 \tql\tx7560 \tql\tx7920 \tql\tx8280 {\f1 \fs28 \b Plugin Developpement Guidelines for Graph32.\par 
}\pard \s4 \qj \sl200 \sb240 \sa60 \tql\tx360 \tql\tx720 \tql\tx1080 \tql\tx1440 \tql\tx1800 \tql\tx2160 \tql\tx2520 \tql\tx2880 \tql\tx3240 \tql\tx3600 \tql\tx3960 \tql\tx4320 \tql\tx4680 \tql\tx5040 \tql\tx5400 \tql\tx5760 \tql\tx6120 \tql\tx6480 \tql\tx6840 \tql\tx7200 \tql\tx7560 \tql\tx7920 \tql\tx8280 {\f1 \b 1). Major guidelines for the plugin\par 
}\pard \s2 \qj \sl200 \sa100 \tql\tx360 \tql\tx720 \tql\tx1080 \tql\tx1440 \tql\tx1800 \tql\tx2160 \tql\tx2520 \tql\tx2880 \tql\tx3240 \tql\tx3600 \tql\tx3960 \tql\tx4320 \tql\tx4680 \tql\tx5040 \tql\tx5400 \tql\tx5760 \tql\tx6120 \tql\tx6480 \tql\tx6840 \tql\tx7200 \tql\tx7560 \tql\tx7920 \tql\tx8280 {\f1 \fs20 \par 
}\pard \s5 \qj \sl200 \sa100 \tql\tx360 \tql\tx720 \tql\tx1080 \tql\tx1440 \tql\tx1800 \tql\tx2160 \tql\tx2520 \tql\tx2880 \tql\tx3240 \tql\tx3600 \tql\tx3960 \tql\tx4320 \tql\tx4680 \tql\tx5040 \tql\tx5400 \tql\tx5760 \tql\tx6120 \tql\tx6480 \tql\tx6840 \tql\tx7200 \tql\tx7560 \tql\tx7920 \tql\tx8280 {\f1 \fs20 \b \tab a). Unique Plugin Identifier (UPI)\par 
}\pard \s2 \qj \sl200 \sa100 \tql\tx360 \tql\tx720 \tql\tx1080 \tql\tx1440 \tql\tx1800 \tql\tx2160 \tql\tx2520 \tql\tx2880 \tql\tx3240 \tql\tx3600 \tql\tx3960 \tql\tx4320 \tql\tx4680 \tql\tx5040 \tql\tx5400 \tql\tx5760 \tql\tx6120 \tql\tx6480 \tql\tx6840 \tql\tx7200 \tql\tx7560 \tql\tx7920 \tql\tx8280 {\f1 \fs20 \tab You will need a Unique Plugin Identifier for each plugin you develop for Graph32. The UPI is a two digits number that will be used by Graph32 to identify your plugin's .opo and .rsc file and also it's folder. The UPI should also be present into all the gl}{\f1 \fs20 obals you will declare as well as into all procedures name. It is used in order not to get any problems with the plugins globals interfering with Graph32's globals.\par 
}\pard \s2 \qj \sl200 \sa100 \tql\tx360 \tql\tx720 \tql\tx1080 \tql\tx1440 \tql\tx1800 \tql\tx2160 \tql\tx2520 \tql\tx2880 \tql\tx3240 \tql\tx3600 \tql\tx3960 \tql\tx4320 \tql\tx4680 \tql\tx5040 \tql\tx5400 \tql\tx5760 \tql\tx6120 \tql\tx6480 \tql\tx6840 \tql\tx7200 \tql\tx7560 \tql\tx7920 \tql\tx8280 {\f1 \fs20 \tab You can get a UPI for your plugin by mailing me a short description of your plugin at npiguet@hotmail.com\par 
}\pard \s5 \qj \sl200 \sa100 \tql\tx360 \tql\tx720 \tql\tx1080 \tql\tx1440 \tql\tx1800 \tql\tx2160 \tql\tx2520 \tql\tx2880 \tql\tx3240 \tql\tx3600 \tql\tx3960 \tql\tx4320 \tql\tx4680 \tql\tx5040 \tql\tx5400 \tql\tx5760 \tql\tx6120 \tql\tx6480 \tql\tx6840 \tql\tx7200 \tql\tx7560 \tql\tx7920 \tql\tx8280 {\f1 \fs20 \b \tab b). General procedure and variable names\par 
}\pard \s2 \qj \sl200 \sa100 \tql\tx360 \tql\tx720 \tql\tx1080 \tql\tx1440 \tql\tx1800 \tql\tx2160 \tql\tx2520 \tql\tx2880 \tql\tx3240 \tql\tx3600 \tql\tx3960 \tql\tx4320 \tql\tx4680 \tql\tx5040 \tql\tx5400 \tql\tx5760 \tql\tx6120 \tql\tx6480 \tql\tx6840 \tql\tx7200 \tql\tx7560 \tql\tx7920 \tql\tx8280 {\f1 \fs20 \tab It is important to use the naming convention described below for all your variables. Local variables can be named as you wish, but it is better to use the same naming convention as for global variable. All of you gobals should be named as follows: \par 
}\pard \s2 \ql \sl200 \sa100 \tql\tx360 \tql\tx720 \tql\tx1080 \tql\tx1440 \tql\tx1800 \tql\tx2160 \tql\tx2520 \tql\tx2880 \tql\tx3240 \tql\tx3600 \tql\tx3960 \tql\tx4320 \tql\tx4680 \tql\tx5040 \tql\tx5400 \tql\tx5760 \tql\tx6120 \tql\tx6480 \tql\tx6840 \tql\tx7200 \tql\tx7560 \tql\tx7920 \tql\tx8280 {\f1 \fs20 VariableNameXX%\tab for an integer}\line {\f1 \fs20 VariableNameXX&\tab for a long integer}\line {\f1 \fs20 VariableNameXX\tab for a floting point number}\line {\f1 \fs20 VariableNameXX$\tab for a string\par 
}\pard \s2 \qj \sl200 \sa100 \tql\tx360 \tql\tx720 \tql\tx1080 \tql\tx1440 \tql\tx1800 \tql\tx2160 \tql\tx2520 \tql\tx2880 \tql\tx3240 \tql\tx3600 \tql\tx3960 \tql\tx4320 \tql\tx4680 \tql\tx5040 \tql\tx5400 \tql\tx5760 \tql\tx6120 \tql\tx6480 \tql\tx6840 \tql\tx7200 \tql\tx7560 \tql\tx7920 \tql\tx8280 {\f1 \fs20 \tab In all of those cases,}{\f1 \fs20 \i  XX}{\f1 \fs20  should be you UPI. Example: the matrix calculator plugin has the UPI 01 thus a valid name for one of it's globals would be }{\f1 \fs20 \i matrix01&.}{\f1 \fs20  Your procedures should follow the same naming convention as your global variables. This is very important, it makes sure that you global variables name and procedures name does not interfere with Graph32's or other plugin's variables name or procedures na}{\f1 \fs20 me.\par 
}\pard \s5 \qj \sl200 \sa100 \tql\tx360 \tql\tx720 \tql\tx1080 \tql\tx1440 \tql\tx1800 \tql\tx2160 \tql\tx2520 \tql\tx2880 \tql\tx3240 \tql\tx3600 \tql\tx3960 \tql\tx4320 \tql\tx4680 \tql\tx5040 \tql\tx5400 \tql\tx5760 \tql\tx6120 \tql\tx6480 \tql\tx6840 \tql\tx7200 \tql\tx7560 \tql\tx7920 \tql\tx8280 {\f1 \fs20 \b \tab c). Required procedures\par 
}\pard \s2 \qj \sl200 \sa100 \tql\tx360 \tql\tx720 \tql\tx1080 \tql\tx1440 \tql\tx1800 \tql\tx2160 \tql\tx2520 \tql\tx2880 \tql\tx3240 \tql\tx3600 \tql\tx3960 \tql\tx4320 \tql\tx4680 \tql\tx5040 \tql\tx5400 \tql\tx5760 \tql\tx6120 \tql\tx6480 \tql\tx6840 \tql\tx7200 \tql\tx7560 \tql\tx7920 \tql\tx8280 {\f1 \fs20 \tab Graph32 will call 4 different procedure which must be defined in you plugin, those procedures are:\par 
}\pard \s2 \qj \sl200 \sa100 \tql\tx360 \tql\tx720 \tql\tx1080 \tql\tx1440 \tql\tx1800 \tql\tx2160 \tql\tx2520 \tql\tx2880 \tql\tx3240 \tql\tx3600 \tql\tx3960 \tql\tx4320 \tql\tx4680 \tql\tx5040 \tql\tx5400 \tql\tx5760 \tql\tx6120 \tql\tx6480 \tql\tx6840 \tql\tx7200 \tql\tx7560 \tql\tx7920 \tql\tx8280 {\f1 \fs20 \tab }{\f1 \fs20 \i menuXX:}\line {\f1 \fs20 \i \tab initXX:(proc$,number%)}\line {\f1 \fs20 \i \tab clearXX:}\line {\f1 \fs20 \i \tab returnNameXX$:}{\f1 \fs20 \par 
}\pard \s2 \qj \sl200 \sa100 \tql\tx360 \tql\tx720 \tql\tx1080 \tql\tx1440 \tql\tx1800 \tql\tx2160 \tql\tx2520 \tql\tx2880 \tql\tx3240 \tql\tx3600 \tql\tx3960 \tql\tx4320 \tql\tx4680 \tql\tx5040 \tql\tx5400 \tql\tx5760 \tql\tx6120 \tql\tx6480 \tql\tx6840 \tql\tx7200 \tql\tx7560 \tql\tx7920 \tql\tx8280 {\f1 \fs20 where XX is your plugin's UPI. }{\f1 \fs20 \i menuXX:}{\f1 \fs20  is used when the user wishes to use your plugin, it should contain a menu where all the options of your plugins are defined and they should be acessed so.}{\f1 \fs20 \i \par 
}\pard \s2 \qj \sl200 \sa100 \tql\tx360 \tql\tx720 \tql\tx1080 \tql\tx1440 \tql\tx1800 \tql\tx2160 \tql\tx2520 \tql\tx2880 \tql\tx3240 \tql\tx3600 \tql\tx3960 \tql\tx4320 \tql\tx4680 \tql\tx5040 \tql\tx5400 \tql\tx5760 \tql\tx6120 \tql\tx6480 \tql\tx6840 \tql\tx7200 \tql\tx7560 \tql\tx7920 \tql\tx8280 {\f1 \fs20 \i init01XX:(proc$,number%)}{\f1 \fs20  is used to make sure that your plugin's globals are kept when Graph32 is loaded but does not use your plugin. That means that all globals defined in that procedure will be kept from one plugin access to the other. Globals defined in other procedures will }{\f1 \fs20 be lost from one plugin access to the other. The two parameters are used to link your plugin into Graph32 just as you link the toolbar module. The last line of this procedure MUST be the following :\par 
}\pard \s2 \qj \sl200 \sa100 \tql\tx360 \tql\tx720 \tql\tx1080 \tql\tx1440 \tql\tx1800 \tql\tx2160 \tql\tx2520 \tql\tx2880 \tql\tx3240 \tql\tx3600 \tql\tx3960 \tql\tx4320 \tql\tx4680 \tql\tx5040 \tql\tx5400 \tql\tx5760 \tql\tx6120 \tql\tx6480 \tql\tx6840 \tql\tx7200 \tql\tx7560 \tql\tx7920 \tql\tx8280 {\f1 \fs20 \tab }{\f1 \fs20 \i @(proc$):(num%)}{\f1 \fs20 \par 
}\pard \s2 \qj \sl200 \sa100 \tql\tx360 \tql\tx720 \tql\tx1080 \tql\tx1440 \tql\tx1800 \tql\tx2160 \tql\tx2520 \tql\tx2880 \tql\tx3240 \tql\tx3600 \tql\tx3960 \tql\tx4320 \tql\tx4680 \tql\tx5040 \tql\tx5400 \tql\tx5760 \tql\tx6120 \tql\tx6480 \tql\tx6840 \tql\tx7200 \tql\tx7560 \tql\tx7920 \tql\tx8280 {\f1 \fs20 \tab This links your plugin to Graph32 and makes sure that globals decared into }{\f1 \fs20 \i initXX:(proc$,num%) }{\f1 \fs20 are kept from one plugin access to the other.\par 
}\pard \s2 \qj \sl200 \sa100 \tql\tx360 \tql\tx720 \tql\tx1080 \tql\tx1440 \tql\tx1800 \tql\tx2160 \tql\tx2520 \tql\tx2880 \tql\tx3240 \tql\tx3600 \tql\tx3960 \tql\tx4320 \tql\tx4680 \tql\tx5040 \tql\tx5400 \tql\tx5760 \tql\tx6120 \tql\tx6480 \tql\tx6840 \tql\tx7200 \tql\tx7560 \tql\tx7920 \tql\tx8280 {\f1 \fs20 \tab The procedure }{\f1 \fs20 \i clearXX:}{\f1 \fs20  is called when Graph32 shuts down or when the user unloads your plugin during the execution of Graph32. This procedure should close ALL threads opened by your plugin (ie: help file, files opened in another application etc..)\par 
}\pard \s2 \qj \sl200 \sa100 \tql\tx360 \tql\tx720 \tql\tx1080 \tql\tx1440 \tql\tx1800 \tql\tx2160 \tql\tx2520 \tql\tx2880 \tql\tx3240 \tql\tx3600 \tql\tx3960 \tql\tx4320 \tql\tx4680 \tql\tx5040 \tql\tx5400 \tql\tx5760 \tql\tx6120 \tql\tx6480 \tql\tx6840 \tql\tx7200 \tql\tx7560 \tql\tx7920 \tql\tx8280 {\f1 \fs20 \tab The procedure }{\f1 \fs20 \i returnNameXX:}{\f1 \fs20  is used by Graph32 to get your plugin's name to display it at various places (like in the }{\f1 \fs20 \i File->Plugin}{\f1 \fs20  menu card). It is called only once, when Graph32 loads your plugin.\par 
}\pard \s5 \qj \sl200 \sa100 \tql\tx360 \tql\tx720 \tql\tx1080 \tql\tx1440 \tql\tx1800 \tql\tx2160 \tql\tx2520 \tql\tx2880 \tql\tx3240 \tql\tx3600 \tql\tx3960 \tql\tx4320 \tql\tx4680 \tql\tx5040 \tql\tx5400 \tql\tx5760 \tql\tx6120 \tql\tx6480 \tql\tx6840 \tql\tx7200 \tql\tx7560 \tql\tx7920 \tql\tx8280 {\f1 \fs20 \b \tab d). Naming and placing plugin files\par 
}\pard \s2 \qj \sl200 \sa100 \tql\tx360 \tql\tx720 \tql\tx1080 \tql\tx1440 \tql\tx1800 \tql\tx2160 \tql\tx2520 \tql\tx2880 \tql\tx3240 \tql\tx3600 \tql\tx3960 \tql\tx4320 \tql\tx4680 \tql\tx5040 \tql\tx5400 \tql\tx5760 \tql\tx6120 \tql\tx6480 \tql\tx6840 \tql\tx7200 \tql\tx7560 \tql\tx7920 \tql\tx8280 {\f1 \fs20 \tab All of your plugin's files should be installed into the following folder:\par 
}\pard \s2 \qj \sl200 \sa100 \tql\tx360 \tql\tx720 \tql\tx1080 \tql\tx1440 \tql\tx1800 \tql\tx2160 \tql\tx2520 \tql\tx2880 \tql\tx3240 \tql\tx3600 \tql\tx3960 \tql\tx4320 \tql\tx4680 \tql\tx5040 \tql\tx5400 \tql\tx5760 \tql\tx6120 \tql\tx6480 \tql\tx6840 \tql\tx7200 \tql\tx7560 \tql\tx7920 \tql\tx8280 {\f1 \fs20 \tab }{\f1 \fs20 \i !:\System\Apps\Graph32\XX\\par 
}\pard \s2 \qj \sl200 \sa100 \tql\tx360 \tql\tx720 \tql\tx1080 \tql\tx1440 \tql\tx1800 \tql\tx2160 \tql\tx2520 \tql\tx2880 \tql\tx3240 \tql\tx3600 \tql\tx3960 \tql\tx4320 \tql\tx4680 \tql\tx5040 \tql\tx5400 \tql\tx5760 \tql\tx6120 \tql\tx6480 \tql\tx6840 \tql\tx7200 \tql\tx7560 \tql\tx7920 \tql\tx8280 {\f1 \fs20 \i \tab }{\f1 \fs20 and should be named }{\f1 \fs20 \i XX.opo}{\f1 \fs20  and }{\f1 \fs20 \i XX.rsc}{\f1 \fs20  where }{\f1 \fs20 \i XX}{\f1 \fs20  is your plugin's UPI. }{\f1 \fs20 \i ! }{\f1 \fs20 is the disk on which Graph32 is installed. All other files (help file etc...) must be placed in the same directory but can be named as you wish since it is not Graph32 which will load them. As your plugin should be installed on the same disk as Graph32 you}{\f1 \fs20  can use }{\f1 \fs20 \i diskLetter$}{\f1 \fs20  which is a global variable defined in Graph32 and containing the disk letter on which it is installed.\par 
